<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: AIB's U.S. unit issues $200 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>AIB's U.S. unit issues $200 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allied Irish Banks Plc said on Monday that its U.S. subsidiary First Maryland Bancorp had issued $200 million in fixed rate subordinated notes due July 1, 2007.</p>
<p>The interest rate on the notes, which were issued at a price of 99.943 percent, is fixed at 7.2 percent, AIB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The securities qualify as Tier 2 capital and interest will be payable on January 1 and July 1 of each year commencing on January 1, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
